From 29b6f5b5f0ae19881063fba71eb8cfd6dd5267f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 825/826] fix(serve): bind SSE keep-alive done callback per
 wait to prevent InvalidStateError

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-61-r2's series applied through 0824.

Rationale: Under long idle streams in _keep_alive_stream (vllm/entrypoints/serve/utils/sse_keep_alive.py),
when the keep-alive timer fires and resolves current_waiter to False in the same
event-loop turn that next_task finishes, asyncio queues the shared _on_task_done
callback onto loop._ready before remove_done_callback runs. After synchronously
yielding the keep-alive comment and chunk and creating task_2 with a new
current_waiter, loop._ready invokes the stale callback from task_1, resolving
task_2's waiter to True while task_2 is still pending so next_task.result() raises
asyncio.InvalidStateError: Result is not set. (#1210). Bind each wait's done
callback to its own (waiter, watched_task) pair, guard the wait with
while not next_task.done(), and always detach the callback in finally.

Quality implications: None on model outputs or hot-path token latency. Preserves
the single rolling call_at timer design for fast decode streaming and shields
upstream generator cleanup on client disconnect.

Tests: CPU pytest tests/entrypoints/serve/utils/test_sse_keep_alive_race.py in
the candidate-61-r2 container covering the deterministic same-turn timer/completion
race, fast-stream pass-through, and ASGI StreamingResponse disconnect cleanup.

Upstream status: local fix for #1210.
